s.org/download/downloadnsa?filename=8c33cc0b-ba23-4d3d-9dbe-168e10d5fcfb.pdf&urlslug=plyometrics-for-beginners-basic-considerati","sourceTitle":"Plyometrics for Beginners: Basic Considerations","sourcePublisher":"World Athletics","sourceKind":"governing_body","evidenceQuality":76,"claims":["Force absorption is shared across the foot and ankle, knee, and hip rather than isolated to one joint.","The card should identify plantar flexors and intrinsic foot muscles, quadriceps, hamstrings, gluteals, hip abductors and external rotators, and trunk stabilizers with task-specific primary and secondary roles."]},{"sectionKey":"biomechanics","sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9474351/","sourceTitle":"Biomechanical and Neuromuscular Performance Requirements of Horizontal Deceleration: A Review with Implications for Random Intermittent Multi-Directional Sports","sourcePublisher":"Sports Medicine - Open","sourceKind":"peer_reviewed_research","evidenceQuality":90,"claims":["Effective braking coordinates lower-limb flexion, centre-of-mass control, foot placement, and force direction to attenuate and apply braking force.","Observable quality includes quiet controlled contact, whole-foot pressure, coordinated ankle-knee-hip flexion, knee tracking, stable pelvis and trunk, and ownership of the final position without extra steps."]},{"sectionKey":"difficulty","sourceUrl":"https://www.nsca.com/contentassets/116c55d64e1343d2b264e05aaf158a91/basics_of_strength_and_conditioning_manual.pdf","sourceTitle":"Basics of Strength and Conditioning Manual","sourcePublisher":"National Strength and Conditioning Association","sourceKind":"professional_standard","evidenceQuality":84,"claims":["Plyometric and landing intensity changes with speed, external height, body mass, external load, and task complexity.","Exercise difficulty must score technical complexity and physical demand directly, including coordination, impact, supervision, work capacity, and consequence of error; it must 